#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From: Rutger Nijlunsing <rutger@nospam.com>\n"
"Subject: Setting up a Git repository which can be pushed into and pulled "
"from over HTTP(S).\n"
"Abstract: Setting up a Git repository which can be pushed into\n"
" and pulled from over HTTP(S).\n"
"Date: Thu, 10 Aug 2006 22:00:26 +0200\n"
"Content-type: text/asciidoc\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to setup Git server over http"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:14
msgid ""
"This document is from 2006.  A lot has happened since then, and this "
"document is now relevant mainly if your web host is not CGI capable.  Almost "
"everyone else should instead look at linkgit:git-http-backend[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:20
msgid ""
"Since Apache is one of those packages people like to compile themselves "
"while others prefer the bureaucrat's dream Debian, it is impossible to give "
"guidelines which will work for everyone. Just send some feedback to the "
"mailing list at git@vger.kernel.org to get this document tailored to your "
"favorite distro."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:23
msgid "What's needed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:25
msgid "Have an Apache web-server"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:27
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:40
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:50
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:193
msgid "On Debian:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ apt-get install apache2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:34
msgid ""
"To get apache2 by default started, edit /etc/default/apache2 and set "
"NO_START=0"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:36
msgid "can edit the configuration of it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:38
msgid "This could be found under /etc/httpd, or refer to your Apache documentation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:42
msgid "this means being able to edit files under /etc/apache2"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:44
msgid "can restart it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:48
msgid ""
"`apachectl --graceful` might do. If it doesn't, just stop and restart "
"apache. Be warning that active connections to your server might be aborted "
"by this."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:53
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ /etc/init.d/apache2 restart\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:56
msgid "or"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:59
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ /etc/init.d/apache2 force-reload\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:62
msgid "(which seems to do the same)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:65
msgid ""
"This adds symlinks from the /etc/apache2/mods-enabled to "
"/etc/apache2/mods-available."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:67
msgid "have permissions to chown a directory"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:69
msgid "have Git installed on the client, and"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:72
msgid ""
"either have Git installed on the server or have a webdav client on the "
"client."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:75
msgid ""
"In effect, this means you're going to be root, or that you're using a "
"preconfigured WebDAV server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:78
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: setup a bare Git repository"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:85
msgid ""
"At the time of writing, git-http-push cannot remotely create a Git "
"repository. So we have to do that at the server side with Git. Another "
"option is to generate an empty bare repository at the client and copy it to "
"the server with a WebDAV client (which is the only option if Git is not "
"installed on the server)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:89
msgid ""
"Create the directory under the DocumentRoot of the directories served by "
"Apache. As an example we take /usr/local/apache2, but try \"grep "
"DocumentRoot /where/ever/httpd.conf\" to find your root:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:92
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    $ cd /usr/local/apache/htdocs\n"
"    $ mkdir my-new-repo.git\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:94
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:111
#, no-wrap
msgid "  On Debian:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:97
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    $ cd /var/www\n"
"    $ mkdir my-new-repo.git\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:100
msgid "Initialize a bare repository"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:103
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    $ cd my-new-repo.git\n"
"    $ git --bare init\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:107
msgid ""
"Change the ownership to your web-server's credentials. Use `\"grep ^User "
"httpd.conf\"` and `\"grep ^Group httpd.conf\"` to find out:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:109
#, no-wrap
msgid "    $ chown -R www.www .\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "    $ chown -R www-data.www-data .\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:118
msgid ""
"If you do not know which user Apache runs as, you can alternatively do a "
"\"chmod -R a+w .\", inspect the files which are created later on, and set "
"the permissions appropriately."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:122
msgid ""
"Restart apache2, and check whether http://server/my-new-repo.git gives a "
"directory listing. If not, check whether apache started up successfully."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:125
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: enable DAV on this repository"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:128
msgid "First make sure the dav_module is loaded. For this, insert in httpd.conf:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:131
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    LoadModule dav_module libexec/httpd/libdav.so\n"
"    AddModule mod_dav.c\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:134
msgid ""
"Also make sure that this line exists which is the file used for locking DAV "
"operations:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:136
#, no-wrap
msgid "  DAVLockDB \"/usr/local/apache2/temp/DAV.lock\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:138
#, no-wrap
msgid "  On Debian these steps can be performed with:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:145
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    Enable the dav and dav_fs modules of apache:\n"
"    $ a2enmod dav_fs\n"
"    (just to be sure. dav_fs might be unneeded, I don't know)\n"
"    $ a2enmod dav\n"
"    The DAV lock is located in /etc/apache2/mods-available/dav_fs.conf:\n"
"      DAVLockDB /var/lock/apache2/DAVLock\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:149
msgid ""
"Of course, it can point somewhere else, but the string is actually just a "
"prefix in some Apache configurations, and therefore the _directory_ has to "
"be writable by the user Apache runs as."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:151
msgid "Then, add something like this to your httpd.conf"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:159
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  <Location /my-new-repo.git>\n"
"     DAV on\n"
"     AuthType Basic\n"
"     AuthName \"Git\"\n"
"     AuthUserFile /usr/local/apache2/conf/passwd.git\n"
"     Require valid-user\n"
"  </Location>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:162
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  On Debian:\n"
"    Create (or add to) /etc/apache2/conf.d/git.conf :\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:170
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <Location /my-new-repo.git>\n"
"       DAV on\n"
"       AuthType Basic\n"
"       AuthName \"Git\"\n"
"       AuthUserFile /etc/apache2/passwd.git\n"
"       Require valid-user\n"
"    </Location>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:172
#, no-wrap
msgid "    Debian automatically reads all files under /etc/apache2/conf.d.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:175
msgid ""
"The password file can be somewhere else, but it has to be readable by Apache "
"and preferably not readable by the world."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:178
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create this file by\n"
"    $ htpasswd -c /usr/local/apache2/conf/passwd.git <user>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:181
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    On Debian:\n"
"      $ htpasswd -c /etc/apache2/passwd.git <user>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:185
msgid ""
"You will be asked a password, and the file is created. Subsequent calls to "
"htpasswd should omit the '-c' option, since you want to append to the "
"existing file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:187
msgid "You need to restart Apache."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:191
msgid ""
"Now go to http://<username>@<servername>/my-new-repo.git in your browser to "
"check whether it asks for a password and accepts the right password."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:195
#, no-wrap
msgid "   To test the WebDAV part, do:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:198
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $ apt-get install litmus\n"
"   $ litmus http://<servername>/my-new-repo.git <username> <password>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:200
#, no-wrap
msgid "   Most tests should pass.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:204
msgid ""
"A command-line tool to test WebDAV is cadaver. If you prefer GUIs, for "
"example, konqueror can open WebDAV URLs as \"webdav://...\" or "
"\"webdavs://...\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:208
msgid ""
"If you're into Windows, from XP onwards Internet Explorer supports "
"WebDAV. For this, do Internet Explorer -> Open Location -> "
"http://<servername>/my-new-repo.git [x] Open as webfolder -> login ."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:211
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: setup the client"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:216
msgid ""
"Make sure that you have HTTP support, i.e. your Git was built with libcurl "
"(version more recent than 7.10). The command 'git http-push' with no "
"argument should display a usage message."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:219
msgid ""
"Then, add the following to your $HOME/.netrc (you can do without, but will "
"be asked to input your password a _lot_ of times):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:223
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    machine <servername>\n"
"    login <username>\n"
"    password <password>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:226
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"...and set permissions:\n"
"     chmod 600 ~/.netrc\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:229
msgid ""
"If you want to access the web-server by its IP, you have to type that in, "
"instead of the server name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:231
msgid "To check whether all is OK, do:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:233
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   curl --netrc --location -v "
"http://<username>@<servername>/my-new-repo.git/HEAD\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:236
msgid ""
"...this should give something like 'ref: refs/heads/master', which is the "
"content of the file HEAD on the server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:239
msgid ""
"Now, add the remote in your existing repository which contains the project "
"you want to export:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:242
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $ git-config remote.upload.url \\\n"
"       http://<username>@<servername>/my-new-repo.git/\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:246
msgid ""
"It is important to put the last '/'; Without it, the server will send a "
"redirect which git-http-push does not (yet) understand, and git-http-push "
"will repeat the request infinitely."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:249
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: make the initial push"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:252
msgid "From your client repository, do"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:254
#, no-wrap
msgid "   $ git push upload master\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:258
msgid ""
"This pushes branch 'master' (which is assumed to be the branch you want to "
"export) to repository called 'upload', which we previously defined with "
"git-config."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:261
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using a proxy:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:267
msgid ""
"If you have to access the WebDAV server from behind an HTTP(S) proxy, set "
"the variable 'all_proxy' to `http://proxy-host.com:port`, or "
"`http://login-on-proxy:passwd-on-proxy@proxy-host.com:port`. See 'man curl' "
"for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:270
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:273
msgid "If git-http-push says"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:275
#, no-wrap
msgid "   Error: no DAV locking support on remote repo http://...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:279
msgid ""
"then it means the web-server did not accept your authentication. Make sure "
"that the user name and password matches in httpd.conf, .netrc and the URL "
"you are uploading to."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:284
msgid ""
"If git-http-push shows you an error (22/502) when trying to MOVE a blob, it "
"means that your web-server somehow does not recognize its name in the "
"request; This can happen when you start Apache, but then disable the network "
"interface. A simple restart of Apache helps."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:287
msgid ""
"Errors like (22/502) are of format (curl error code/http error code). So "
"(22/404) means something like 'not found' at the server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:289
msgid "Reading /usr/local/apache2/logs/error_log is often helpful."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:291
#, no-wrap
msgid "  On Debian: Read /var/log/apache2/error.log instead.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:295
msgid ""
"If you access HTTPS locations, Git may fail verifying the SSL certificate "
"(this is return code 60). Setting http.sslVerify=false can help diagnosing "
"the problem, but removes security checks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/howto/setup-git-server-over-http.txt:298
msgid "Debian References: http://www.debian-administration.org/articles/285"
msgstr ""

